course: dictionary
lesson: 5431
title: Lake: a big pool of water
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lake is a big area of water with land all around it. Think of a lake in a park, or in the mountains, with trees and hills around its edge. Most lakes have fresh water, not salty sea water, so you can drink from some of them after cleaning the water.
explain: The word lake can also mean a pool of something else. «A lake of lava» does not mean water at all: it is a pool of hot, melted rock. Always check the words around the word to find which meaning fits.
explain: Read this safety sentence: «The advice of RoSPA is never to go onto ice on ponds, lakes, rivers or canals.» The word lakes is in a list with ponds, rivers and canals. The list tells you that lakes are places of water, and that the warning is about thin, dangerous ice.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it in the sentence. «A lotus seed was grown from a dry lake bed in China.» A dry lake bed is the ground where a lake used to be, now with no water. That makes sense because a lake is water lying in a hollow of the land.
fact: A lake is a big area of water with land all around it.
fact: Most lakes have fresh water, not salty sea water.
fact: «A lake of lava» means a pool of hot, melted rock.
fact: «Lakeside» means the land at the edge of a lake.
fact: Ice on lakes can look solid but may be thin and dangerous, so never go onto it.
exercise: «A lake is a body of water lying in a hollow of the land.» What is a lake? | A hill covered in grass | A salty sea | *A big area of water with land all around it | A river that flows out to the sea
exercise: «The fishermen sat by the lake all morning.» Find and copy the word that tells you where the fishermen sat. | *lake | sat | morning | fishermen
exercise: The safety advice says never to go onto ice on lakes. What is the safe thing to do? | Test it with a big stone | *Keep off the ice | Go out in a big group | Walk across it quickly
test: In «a lake of lava», what does lake mean? | A bird that swims | A cold, icy path | *A pool of something else, here hot melted rock | A deep, dark cave
test: Most lakes have which kind of water? | Melted rock | Hot oil | Salty sea water | *Fresh water
exam: «The lotus seed came from a dry lake bed in China.» What does lake bed mean here? | A boat that sails on a lake | *The ground where a lake used to be | A bed made of water | A bridge over a lake
